I expect so.  Once you can BUC-test (altar, pet, priest-if-you-are-one)
it's easy to pick 'good armor' from 'bad armor' (if it's not cursed,
just *try it*.  You'll be told the +-).  Weapons, not so easy, but watch
how they stack in inventory (if they're stackable -- daggers, arrows,
etc.  +0 will probably be the most common).

> b - I'm carrying everything that seems remotely useful and light; a
> weapon, only the armor I'm wearing, two or three items of food.
> However, the huge amount of unidentified scrolls/potions/gems filled
> the inventory. I've just found a bag in a bones level but I gather
> it's most probably cursed.

Good chance, yes.

If it's a BOH you don't want to pick it up (heavy!) or open it (stuff
goes *poof*!).  Remember where it is, come back.  If you have a way to
remove the curse (if you can pick it up, !oHW or ?oRC will do it, or
/oCancellation if you can't... make sure any goodies in the area of
effect are moved or you'll cancel them, too, and canceling a +7 weapon
makes people cry).

> What's the usual inventory management strategy? Throwing every potion
> to enemies to try the identification? Not taking gems or scrolls until
> I have a way of identifying them?

Gems and scrolls tend to be fairly light, IIRC (at least, it takes a lot
of them to go over).  If I have a sack to put them in I usually do (keep
them out of main).  Price-ID at a store helps a lot.

> c - I'm not sure if I'm in the main cave or not. Is there any way of
> knowing? (is it enough to see if it's "cavelike" or "room+corridor").

The Mines have lots of open spaces, gnomes and dwarves.  If you're not
seeing them, you're probably in the dungeon.  Also, DL10... IIRC
Minetown happens before that, so if you haven't seen Minetown yet you're
not in the Mines.

Given where you are gamewise, I'd go back up, find the other stairs
down, and hit the Mines.  Lots (*lots*!) of armor there, and Minetown
always has a temple.  And if it's not a bones level, there'll be a
priest there too.  And there's always stores.

> d - The most important one. After getting to AC:-7 and getting a few
> xp-levels everything seems much easier than the first 5 levels.

Of course.  You have armor and hit points, and you may be becoming more
skilled with your weapons.

Don't get cocky.

